        "original_id": "8f939340-4a79-5139-a116-ce7d984c0485",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Plant, John Bonham, Phil Collins, Nika Boon, John Baggott, Ian Matthews, Jay Stapley, Carey Willetts\n- Bands/Artists: Led Zeppelin, Massive Attack, Portishead, Kasabian, Pink Floyd, Mike Oldfield, Athlete\n- Events/Projects: Robert Plant tours, Nika Boon album\n\nFacts:\n- John Bonham was born on 31 May 1948 and died on 25 September 1980.\n- John Bonham was an English musician and songwriter best known as the drummer for the British rock band Led Zeppelin.\n- Robert Plant avoided performing Led Zeppelin songs through much of the period discussed on his discography page.\n- Robert Plant's 1983 tour, which featured drummer Phil Collins, was very successful and often played to sold-out arena-sized venues.\n- Robert Plant's 1985 tour was also very successful and often played to sold-out arena-sized venues.\n- Nika Boon was working on a new album planned for release in 2017.\n- Nika Boon's 2017 album project involved collaboration with John Baggott, Ian Matthews, Jay Stapley, and Carey Willetts.\n- John Baggott played keyboards and moogs for Massive Attack, Portishead, and Robert Plant.\n- Ian Matthews was the drummer from Kasabian.\n- Jay Stapley was a guitarist associated with Pink Floyd and Mike Oldfield.\n- Carey Willetts was the bass player from the band Athlete.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
